hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27627","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, he said: Zaynab bint Ka'b narrated to me from Furay'ah bint Malik, she said: My husband went out seeking slaves of his, and he caught up with them at Taraf al-Qadum, and they killed him. Then his death news came to me while I was in a distant house among the houses of my family, so I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, and I said: The news of my husband's death came to me in a distant house among the houses of my family, and he left me neither maintenance nor wealth for his heirs, and the dwelling is not his, so if I moved to my family and my maternal uncles it would be easier for me in some of my affair. He said: Move. Then when I went out to the mosque or to the chamber, he called me or commanded for me and I was called, and he said: Remain in your house in which the news of your husband came to you until the Book reaches its term. She said: So I observed iddah in it for four months and ten days. She said: Then Uthman sent to me and I informed him, and he acted upon it."
"27628","Haddathana Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from Sa'd ibn Ishaq, he said: Zaynab bint Ka'b narrated to me from Furay'ah bint Malik, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, similar to it."
"27907","Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, he said: Sad ibn Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah al-Ansari narrated to us, from his paternal aunt Zaynab bint Kab, that Furayah bint Malik ibn Sinan, the sister of Abu Said al-Khudri, narrated to her that her husband went out seeking some hired laborers of theirs, and he caught up with them at the edge of al-Qadum, and they killed him. His death news came to her while she was in a house of the houses of the Ansar, far from the house of her family, and she disliked observing the waiting period therein, so she came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the news of my husband's death came to me while I am in a house of the houses of the Ansar, far from the houses of my family; he left me only in a dwelling he does not own, and he did not leave me maintenance to be spent upon me, and I did not inherit wealth from him; so if you see fit that I join my brothers and my family, and our affair be together, for that is dearer to me. So he permitted me to join my family. I went out rejoicing at that, until when I was in the chamber or the mosque, he called me, or he ordered with me and I was called. He said to me: How did you claim. So I repeated to him. He said: Remain in the dwelling of your husband in which his death news came to you, until the decree reaches its term. She said: So I observed the waiting period therein for four months and ten days."
